@irevoire  Since MeilisearchHttpError is converted to ResponseError, I found that I need to modify many functions that return ResponseError to add an index_uid parameter and pass it to MeilisearchHttpError. What do you think about this alternative approach?
```rust
trait ErrorWithIndex<T> {
    fn with_index(self, index_uid: &String) -> Result<T, ResponseError>;
}

impl<T> ErrorWithIndex<T> for Result<T, ResponseError> {
    fn with_index(self, index_uid: &String) -> Result<T, ResponseError> {
        self.map_err(|mut error| {
            error.message = format!("Index {}: {}",index_uid, error.message);
            error
        })
    }
}
```
Here is an example
```rust
  let index = index_scheduler.index(&index_uid)?;
  let features = index_scheduler.features();

  let search_kind = search_kind(&query, index_scheduler.get_ref(), &index, features)?;
  let retrieve_vector = RetrieveVectors::new(query.retrieve_vectors, features)?;
  let permit = search_queue.try_get_search_permit().await?;
  let search_result = tokio::task::spawn_blocking(move || {
      perform_search(&index, query, search_kind, retrieve_vector, index_scheduler.features())
          .with_index(&index_uid)
  })
```
